    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0437" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg427"/>

                <head>Laird Brothers to Captain
                        Inglefield, H. M. S. Majestic.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Birkenhead Iron Works,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Birkenhead,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 28, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to the conversation you had with
                    our Mr. John Laird, jun., this morning, and the request you made to us for
                    assistance in preparing the El Monnassir for removal from our graving dock, we
                    shall feel obliged if you will put your request in writing, and we will then
                    give it our best consideration.</p>
                <p>We are, sir, your obedient servants,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LAIRD BROTHERS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Captain <hi rendition="#small-caps">Inglefield,</hi> R. N., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">H. M. S. Majestic.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
